---
title: Fiery Ginger Wings
servings: 12
description: Baked, not fried, and tossed in a sweet gingery sauce with a serious kick, these are The Dude Diet's answer to your chicken wing prayers. If you decide to double or triple the recipe for a large crew, consider separating the flats and drumettes and making the fiery ginger sauce up to a day in advance. Then all you'll have to do come party time is pop the wings in the oven, reheat the sauce, and field endless compliments on your finger food domination.
source: The Dude Diet
tags: Wings
---

= Wings =
Preheat the oven to 400°F.
Line two large #baking sheets{} with aluminum foil.
Spray 2 wire racks with cooking spray and place them on top of the prepared baking sheets.
(If not using wire racks, flip the wings half way through the cooking time.)

Start by prepping the chicken wings.
Remove and discard the wing tips, then separate the wings into flats and drumettes.

Place the @chicken wings{3%lb} into a #large bowl{}.
Drizzle with @sesame oil{1%tbsp} and sprinkle with @salt and @pepper.
Toss to coat.

Arrange the wings on the sprayed wire racks, leaving a little bit of space between each one.
Bake for ~{45%minutes} or until golden brown.

= Sauce =
About 10 minutes before the wings are done, whisk together the @ginger beer{1/2%cup}(non-alcoholic),
@honey{3%tbsp}, @soy sauce{2%tbsp}(low-sodium), @sriracha{4%tsp}, @garlic{2%cloves}(minced),
and @cornstarch{1%tsp} in a #medium bowl{}.

Heat a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat.
When hot, pour in the sauce and bring it to a boil.
Lower to a simmer and cook for ~{5%minutes} or until syrupy.
Remove the skillet from the heat.

Transfer the cooked wings to the skillet with the sauce and toss to coat.
Depending on the size of your pan, you may need to do this in two batches.

= Serving =
{ile your wings on a large plate or #platter.
Drizzle with any extra sauce from the pan, sprinkle with @scallions{2}(finely chopped), and serve warm.
